        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.8\\times0.765=0.612$.",
          "worked": "For each choice of the first digit, put the remaining digits in descending order to maximise the second factor.\n$$\\begin{align*}0.5\\times0.876&=0.438\\\\0.6\\times0.875&=0.525\\\\0.7\\times0.865&=0.6055\\\\0.8\\times0.765&=0.612\\end{align*}$$\nThe greatest product is $0.612$.",
