        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.85\\times0.76=0.646$ (either factor order).",
          "worked": "For each pair of digits, placing the larger digit in the tenths position makes that factor larger. There are three ways to split the four digits into two pairs, ignoring factor order. Compare the greatest product for each split.\n$$\\begin{align*}0.87\\times0.65&=\\frac{87\\times65}{10000}=0.5655\\\\0.86\\times0.75&=\\frac{86\\times75}{10000}=0.645\\\\0.85\\times0.76&=\\frac{85\\times76}{10000}=0.646\\end{align*}$$\nThe greatest product is $0.646$, using $0.85$ and $0.76$ in either order.",
